Don't compile the Windows .rc files under a Ninja generator. CMake's
"Ninja Multi-Config" generator forwards -DCMAKE_INTDIR=\"release\" to rc.exe,
which cannot parse the escaped quotes and stops with
"fatal error RC1107: invalid usage". These .rc files only carry version
resources -- inert in the static libraries this module links, and on
PhysXGpu_64.dll only metadata nothing reads -- so they are marked
HEADER_FILE_ONLY and left out of the compile. Visual Studio generator builds
are unaffected.

A Ninja generator is what the vc15win64-godot presets use: CMake's
"Visual Studio 15 2017" generator needs a registered VS 2017 installation,
which a packman-provided MSVC 14.16 toolchain is not.

diff --git a/physx/source/compiler/cmake/windows/PhysX.cmake b/physx/source/compiler/cmake/windows/PhysX.cmake
index d5561c1..f05dac7 100644
--- a/physx/source/compiler/cmake/windows/PhysX.cmake
+++ b/physx/source/compiler/cmake/windows/PhysX.cmake
@@ -54,6 +54,14 @@ SET(PHYSX_RESOURCE
 	${PHYSX_SOURCE_DIR}/compiler/windows/resource/resource.h
 )
 SOURCE_GROUP(resource FILES ${PHYSX_RESOURCE})
+# CMake's "Ninja Multi-Config" generator forwards -DCMAKE_INTDIR=\"release\" to
+# rc.exe, which cannot parse the escaped quotes and dies with RC1107. These .rc
+# files only carry DLL version info and are inert in a static-library build, so
+# keep them listed but don't compile them when generating for Ninja.
+IF(CMAKE_GENERATOR MATCHES "Ninja")
+	SET_SOURCE_FILES_PROPERTIES(${PHYSX_SOURCE_DIR}/compiler/windows/resource/PhysX.rc PROPERTIES HEADER_FILE_ONLY TRUE)
+ENDIF()
+
 
 SET(PHYSX_DEVICE_SOURCE
 )
